\section{Conclusion}
While Beryllium remains the optimal choice for pure neutron reflection due to its low absorption cross-section, the assembly of an enhanced radiation device often requires a hybrid approach. The integration of $\text{U-238}$ or $\text{W}$ provides the necessary inertial tamping to sustain the reaction, while elements like $\text{Li}$ allow for integrated fuel breeding, thereby enhancing the total device efficiency.

